
# PENDING — this section is deliberately empty.
#
# makeResult needs a ctx carrying a constructed Spec AND Result, built via the
# SDK's own NewSpec/NewResult constructors, plus the absent-error path for
# each. The runner builds ctx from a literal map and has no constructor hook,
# so these cannot be expressed here yet — covered per-language today (e.g.
# go's makeResult-basic / -no-spec / -no-result), which is exactly the drift
# this corpus exists to remove. Promoting it needs a runner change, not just
# fixture data.
#
# An empty `set` runs ZERO cases. Runners must not treat that as a pass by
# accident: `basic: pending` below is the MACHINE-READABLE form of this note,
# so the guard travels into test.json with the fixture instead of living only
# in a comment the consumer never sees.

basic: pending: 'Needs a ctx carrying a Spec AND Result built via the SDK constructors; the runner builds ctx from a literal map and has no constructor hook.'
basic: set: []
